      "content": "yeah, definitely want that urgency. but i'm a bit worried about the legality/trust if we say \"only 5 left\" when we actually have plenty. if we use a countdown or scarcity pricing, how much of a \"stock warning\" should we actually show to the customers? should we be strictly accurate with real-time levels, or is it better to simulate a lower number to keep the conversion rate up?",
